        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 元",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "元 — yuán — \"yuan\", the unit of money, as it is written."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "一本书十元 yì běn shū shí yuán — A book costs ten yuan."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "On a price list it is written 元 (yuán); aloud, most people say kuài: shí kuài. The next lesson puts the character in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "元 (yuán) is inherited from Middle Chinese ngjwon (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), glossed 'great; the beginning; the head'. The unit of money is a modern sense, assumed here, not quoted."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The number, then 元 (yuán): 十元. A thing's price follows the thing: 一本书, 十元."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "When you say it, swap in kuài: yì běn shū shí kuài. 一 falls before the dip of běn: yì běn."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "yuán",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *yuán*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "yuán, once more",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *yuán*, once more]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "一本书十元 — yì běn shū shí yuán — A book costs ten yuan.",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: 一本书十元 — *yì běn shū shí yuán* — A book costs ten yuan.]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "yì běn shū shí kuài — the same price, as people say it",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *yì běn shū shí kuài* — the same price, as people say it]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "say kuài, then 元 (yuán)",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: say *kuài*, then 元]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 5,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does 元 (yuán) mean? (Yuan, as written.) How do people say it aloud? (kuài.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
