          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "jiàqián is built from jià 'price' and qián 'money', the word you know. Both are inherited from Middle Chinese, kaeH and dzjen (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), glossed 'price; value' and 'coin'. The jià of fàngjià, a holiday, sounds the same and is a different word."
            }
          ]
